## 7. Feature-Level Target State

Workers should operate as a production queue system: durable jobs, typed handlers, queues, priorities, leases, heartbeats, retries, DLQs, idempotency, and operational visibility. The CLI and deployment manifests should run the real worker. APIs should expose queue status, stuck jobs, replay, cancel, and worker health. Runtime and saga execution should dispatch side effects through this worker layer or a proven durable backend. Tests should cover multi-worker races, restart recovery, retry exhaustion, and deployment smoke.

